00-first: reading="I can keep track of the books I've read this year.\nWhy: I usually forget what I read by december.\nDone when: I can see them all in one place with a short note on what I thought of each one.\nKeep: a short note on what I thought of each one.\nAvoid: nothing fancy." focused=null
00-first: reading="New users can receive onboarding emails without feeling spammed, during the first week.\nWhy: five emails arrive in the first week and the unsubscribe rate keeps going up.\nDone when: new users do not feel spammed.\nKeep: marketing value; onboarding emails.\nAvoid: killing the emails entirely." focused={"id":"model-ff561e1263021b92","text":"Should the main change be fewer emails, less annoying emails, or another way to keep new users from feeling spammed?"}
00-first: reading="Learners can understand why they got something wrong, on phones.\nWhy: learners currently see a red X and move on; people feel dumb and leave.\nDone when: learners leave a wrong answer feeling smarter not dumber.\nKeep: no gamification.\nAvoid: one more chatbot nobody asked for; rebuilding the whole quiz engine." focused={"id":"model-57692293e9b1bea0","text":"After a wrong answer, what should learners be able to do: understand the explanation, try again with more confidence, or something else?"}
00-first: reading="I can know whether yesterday went well or not within like 5 seconds, in the morning when I open Tinkery.\nWhy: the ledger report is useless to me; its a wall of numbers and i dont know what to do with it; the 6am job sometimes fails silently.\nDone when: yesterday went well or not is clear in like 5 seconds.\nKeep: useful changes per hour; cost maybe.\nAvoid: a dashboard; silent failures." focused={"id":"model-132a657ca6c40234","text":"Does cost need to be part of the morning signal, or is useful changes per hour the one that matters?"}
01-answer: reading="I can know whether yesterday went well or not within like 5 seconds, in the morning when I open Tinkery.\nWhy: the ledger report is useless to me; its a wall of numbers and i dont know what to do with it; the 6am job sometimes fails silently and i only find out days later.\nDone when: yesterday went well or not is clear in like 5 seconds; a failed job overrides everything.\nKeep: useful changes per hour; cost only if its way off.\nAvoid: a dashboard; silent failures." focused=null
